course: dictionary
lesson: 4024
title: Words that name a doer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you what a person or animal does. The ending -er often means one who does the action: a gatherer is one who gathers, or collects things. Once you know gather, you can work out gatherer.
explain: «Hunter-gatherers knew all that by heart, along with hundreds of plants and animals.» The clues are hunter and gatherers. A hunter catches animals and a gatherer collects plants, so hunter-gatherers do both to get food.
explain: The dash joins two jobs into one word. «For most of human history people were hunter-gatherers who hunted, fished and gathered berries, nuts and roots, moving camp with the seasons.» Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: it still makes sense, so you have found it.
fact: A gatherer is a person or animal that collects things, such as food, information or people.
fact: Hunter-gatherers lived by hunting animals and collecting wild plants, nuts and berries instead of farming.
fact: Stone Age people were hunter-gatherers before farming began.
fact: A news gatherer collects news, and a data gatherer collects information.
fact: Some groups still live partly this way today.
exercise: «For most of human history people were hunter-gatherers who hunted, fished and gathered berries, nuts and roots.» What is a hunter-gatherer? | A farmer with lots of cows | A machine that picks up litter | Someone who sells shoes in a market | *A person who hunts animals and collects wild food instead of farming
exercise: A news gatherer is someone who what? | *Collects news | Builds bridges over rivers | Sleeps all day in a tent | Cooks food for a big family
exercise: The word gatherer comes from which word? | garden | *gather | hunter | ring
test: The sentence says hunter-gatherers moved camp with the seasons. What does that suggest? | They lived on the moon | They never moved at all | *They moved camp as the seasons changed | They only lived in houses
test: Stone Age people were hunter-gatherers before what began? | cars | schools | trains | *farming
exam: Which is the best meaning of gatherer? | Someone who never stops talking | Someone who swims in the sea | A large building with many rooms | *Someone or something that collects things
